-- The same program as `unwrap_warning.sdx`, suppressed — plan 38 §1.3 and
-- plan 53 leaf 4.
--
-- Its expectation is **empty**, which is the only way to prove suppression
-- works: a corpus entry that asserts nothing is printed.
--
-- The marker is an **attribute**, and it is consumed. Plan 38 §1.3 rejected
-- both attribute routes together: `#[allow(unwrap)]` passed through makes
-- rustc say `unknown lint`, and `#[redox::allow(unwrap)]` passed through is
-- worse — `error[E0433]: cannot find module or crate 'redox'`, a hard error.
-- Neither objection survives an attribute Redox **drops**, because nothing
-- reaches rustc at all, which is also why no unstable `register_tool` is
-- needed. What it costs is one carve-out in plan 18 §1.3's
-- attributes-are-trivia rule, paid knowingly: plan 48 found `redox fmt`
-- deleting comments from a `.sdx`, so semantics in a comment is semantics a
-- formatter run can remove.
--
-- Criterion 5 wants both halves, so there are two declarations: one with the
-- attribute leading a **statement**, one with it leading the **declaration**,
-- where it covers every call site in the body.
main : ()
main =
  #[redox::allow(unwrap)]
  port = (Some 7).unwrap ()
  print port
  print (port_of (Some 9))

#[redox::allow(unwrap)]
port_of : Option<u64> -> u64
port_of raw =
  first = raw.unwrap ()
  second = (Some 1).expect ("set by construction")
  first + second
